{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CentreGradingObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CentreGradingObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoFiltrationBridge"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.coxeter_reading_excluded_at_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.coxeter_reading_excluded_at_four","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CentreGradingObstruction.lean#L131-L149","doc":"**No shift of the `n = 4` partition grading is the centre's Coxeter-length\ngrading.**\n\nThe word side enters as hypotheses — the exact computed sequence\n`[1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 2, 1]`, stated pointwise for the three degrees the argument\nuses. Everything else is derived.\n\n**Not vacuous.** Concluding `False` from a hypothesis set is a refutation, not a\ntautology, precisely because each part is separately satisfiable: `W = ![1,0,0,0,1,2,1]`\nis realised (it is the measured graded sequence), and `hshift` is realised by\n`W = fun k => N4 (k + c)` for any `c`. What is impossible is their conjunction —\nwhich is the statement that the measured centre grading is a re-indexing of the\npartition grading. All three `W`-hypotheses are used in the proof term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.N4_gapfree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.N4_gapfree","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CentreGradingObstruction.lean#L125-L129","doc":"`N4` is gap-free: its support `{3, 4}` is an interval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.N4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.N4","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CentreGradingObstruction.lean#L121-L123","doc":"The `n = 4` partition-depth multiplicity function, read off `gbDepth_p22`\n(`[2,2] ↦ 3`) and `gbDepth_p4` (`[4] ↦ 4`, shared by all four hooks). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.shift_cannot_fill_a_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.shift_cannot_fill_a_gap","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CentreGradingObstruction.lean#L85-L105","doc":"**A shift of a gap-free multiplicity function is gap-free, so it cannot be\na function with an interior hole.**\n\n`hgapfree` says `N`'s support is order-convex: nothing vanishes strictly between\ntwo nonzero values. `hshift` is the candidate re-indexing. The remaining three\nhypotheses describe the word side: nonzero at degree `0` (the unit is central\nand has filtration degree `0`), **zero at degree `1`**, and nonzero somewhere\nabove (the centre has dimension `p(n) ≥ 2`, so it is not exhausted by the unit).\n\nNo such `c` exists. The proof is three lines and uses every hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CentreGradingObstruction.lean#L69-L71","doc":"The degree-`0` partition stratum is empty: no nonempty diagram has depth `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gbDepth_pos","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CentreGradingObstruction.lean#L53-L67","doc":"**`gbDepth` is positive on every nonempty diagram.**\n\nThe corner hook `λ₁ + λ'₁ - 1` is at least `1 + 1 - 1`. Small, but it is the\nwhole of the degree-`0` obstruction: whatever filtration `J^•` turns out to be,\nits induced grading on `Z(H_n(q))` has `Z^(0) ∋ 1 ≠ 0`, because the unit is\ncentral and lies in filtration degree `0` in *any* algebra filtration. The\npartition side's degree-`0` stratum, by contrast, is empty — so the two cannot\nagree at `k = 0`, for any `n ≥ 1` and any candidate `J^•`.\n\nThis is why the repair has to be a shift, and §2 is why a shift does not work. ","signatureChunk":0}]}